    "created_at": "2020-01-08T18:46:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-08T18:46:54Z",
    "body": "This came up a while ago in #653, at the time we concluded that it was out of scope of starship to parse name of the cluster since the user could just rename the clusters in the kubeconfig file locally. However maybe we should revisit this if it is a feature that a lot of users would want.\r\n\r\nIf this is a feature that users want then we need to think about how we are going to implement it. We could either write a parser for the different Cloud Providers but given the number of providers that exists long term this might be quite complicated and hard to support all of them but this would be easier for the users to use. The other option we could try is to adding a user configured table of aliases to the starship config similar to the [`region_aliases` in the AWS module](https://starship.rs/config/#aws) this would be simpler and quicker to add but every cluster would need to be added to the startship config which if someone is using dynamically provisioned clusters this would be a bit of a painful for them.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
