    "created_at": "2020-01-16T16:15:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-16T16:16:36Z",
    "body": "@andytom #653 is only taking into account kubernetes, but in the case of GKE, that's `gcloud` that is configuring kubernetes clusters and namespace. And other tools need to read these information to match whats configured google side.\r\n\r\nSo I think it should be nice to have a way to parse this value. I believe @romkatv did a great job [there](https://github.com/romkatv/powerlevel10k/blob/8ef2b737d1f6099966a1eb16bdfc90d67b367f22/config/p10k-lean.zsh#L733-L770). Regarding the number of cloud providers, supporting only the significant one by default would be good, and having a way to extend it even better.\r\nI'm not sure how this could be put in place for a tool like starship though.",
