    "body": "For future work post #851 / #839 here's a sample of my configuration, if that helps.\r\nThis was configured by `gcloud` command line tools.\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\napiVersion: v1\r\nclusters:\r\n- cluster:\r\n    certificate-authority-data: ...\r\n    server: https://10.10.10.10\r\n  name: gke_infra-cluster-ada4c490_europe-west1_cluster-1\r\n\r\ncontexts:\r\n- context:\r\n    cluster: gke_infra-cluster-ada4c490_europe-west1_cluster-1\r\n    namespace: trust\r\n    user: gke_infra-cluster-ada4c490_europe-west1_cluster-1\r\n  name: gke_infra-cluster-ada4c490_europe-west1_cluster-1\r\n\r\nusers:\r\n- name: gke_infra-cluster-ada4c490_europe-west1_cluster-1\r\n  user:\r\n    auth-provider:\r\n      config:\r\n        access-token: ...\r\n        cmd-args: config config-helper --format=json\r\n        cmd-path: /usr/local/Caskroom/google-cloud-sdk/latest/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud\r\n        expiry: ...\r\n        expiry-key: '{.credential.token_expiry}'\r\n        token-key: '{.credential.access_token}'\r\n      name: gcp\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd the shortening of the cluster name would be `cluster-1`.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
