    "body": "Since @andytom was so nice to mention this issue to me, I thought might also join this discussion and promote my PR (https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/1015).\r\n\r\nI think context aliases are the way to go for the following reasons:\r\n* it is simple.\r\n* there is a (ready to merge?) PR for it.\r\n* And most importantly: If you are not using one of the managed kubernetes clusters (i.e. by using kops) there is no imposed structure or naming scheme in the cluster name. Hence any automated shortening will fall ...short.\r\n* Alternatively: think of something to accommodate both use cases; automated (if there is structure) and aliases (if not). In that case, I'd still recommend merging my PR as a first step in this direction.\r\n\r\nPerhaps there can be some sort of command in the starship config module to add the current cluster key in to the config alias section.",
