    "updated_at": "2020-04-01T18:21:37Z",
    "body": "I've been thinking about this a little bit over the last few days. I can see times where it would make sense to use them both of the two proposed solutions at the same time, for example, you might have multiple production clusters each one in a different region.\r\n\r\nSo starship would try to parse the name of the cluster and get the short name of the cluster, then either the short or full cluster name could then be looked up in the alias table. What do you guys thing?",
