    "updated_at": "2020-07-15T07:53:05Z",
    "body": "I would love to have at least `context_aliases` be more dynamic, e.g. function at least.\r\nAt this point in time, we have static example documented.\r\n```toml\r\n[kubernetes.context_aliases]\r\n\"dev.local.cluster.k8s\" = \"dev\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhich means\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[kubernetes.context_aliases]\r\n\"arn:aws:eks:region:account:cluster/someproject-prod-cluster\" = \"someproject-prod-cluster-eks\"\r\n\"devopshft-cloud-some-stage\" = \"someproject-stage-cluster-openshift\"\r\n\"gke-dev-cluster-default-pool-e5f5\" = \"someproject-dev-cluster-gke\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhy not to provide a function at least, that can help with parsing it? I have around 50+ clusters,\r\nand they are addded and removed pretty much daily/weekly. It probably there, but not documented. \r\nAs well as something like strip, or regex support nice to have there.",
