    "updated_at": "2020-11-18T15:56:11Z",
    "body": "I love the idea to have more dynamic context_aliases, maybe with wildcards. My current context in the .kube/config looks like this:\r\n\r\n`current-context: namespace/api-clustername-domain-com:port/username`\r\n\r\nSo a context_alias could look like this for example:\r\n\\*api\\-**clustername**\\-domain\\* = **clustername**\r\n\r\nWould be greate if the solution to be developped would also make it possible to shorten this current context to \"clustername\" only, and maybe keeping \"username\" too. The namespaces is added in \"( )\" by the kubernetes module anyways, which is nice.\r\n\r\n@andytom Thank you for merging my issue to this one.\r\n\r\nThank you very much",
